The Constitution makes clear that elections are run by states, so it’s not surprising that the Supreme Court rejected Donald Trump’s attempt to interfere with our vote by mail system. Trump's loss at our nation’s highest court affirms that Oregonians will continue to vote by mail this fall. Thank you to our Attorney General, Secretary of State, and all Oregonians who have worked tirelessly to protect vote by mail and keep our elections, safe, secure, and accurate.

